# Context

## Background
The vendored conformance corpus (next commit) found these six defects
on its first triage run. Each failure was reproduced as a failing unit
test at the exported boundary before the fix, following the same
pattern as the two review findings fixed earlier the same day.

## Gotchas
- The "counts contains matches as evaluated items" test initially
  asserted the wrong expectation: the suite confirms that only items
  MATCHING contains count as evaluated, so [1, 2, "foo"] under
  contains {type: string} is invalid. The suite corrected the author,
  not the other way round.
- multipleOf overflow rejects by suite decree ("always invalid, but
  naive implementations may raise an overflow error"): the true
  quotient may be an exact multiple mathematically, but double
  precision cannot confirm it, so it rejects.
- canonicalKey sorts object keys recursively; jsonScalarEquals already
  did this for enum and const, and uniqueItems was the odd one out.
